course: dictionary
lesson: 9915
title: Tame: animals, stories and dull things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Tame animals» means animals that are not wild and are not afraid of people. «A tame ending» means an ending that is dull and not exciting. Same word, different meaning, and the context is the clue.
explain: Tame can also be a doing word. To tame a wild animal means to train it to live with people. «In stories, a hero tames a horse» tells you the hero trains the horse so it will obey. Tame can also mean to control something strong or wild.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The dog was the first animal people tamed» means people trained it to live with them, and that fits. Be careful, though: an animal can seem tame and still bite, so tame does not always mean safe.
fact: Tame, when it describes an animal, means not wild and not afraid of people.
fact: Tame, as a verb, means to train a wild animal to live with people and obey them.
fact: Tame can also mean dull and not exciting, as in «a tame ending».
fact: People tamed guinea pigs in the Andes thousands of years ago, and they reached Europe on ships about five hundred years ago.
fact: «Not every animal can be tamed.» Wild animals in parks are never tame, so keep your distance from them.
exercise: «In Siberia scientists bred only the tamest foxes.» What does tamest mean here? | Biggest and strongest | Wildest and most dangerous | Fastest runners | *Least afraid of people, the friendliest
exercise: A story has «a tame ending». What does tame mean here? | Sad and dramatic | Loud and noisy | Happy and full of surprises | *Dull and not exciting
exercise: «In stories, a hero tames a horse.» What does tames mean here? | To ride the horse very slowly | *To train a wild animal to live with people | To make the horse a dull colour | To feed the horse once a day
test: «People in the Andes tamed guinea pigs thousands of years ago.» What does tamed mean here? | Hid from people in the hills | Painted them in bright colours | *Trained wild animals to live with people | Cooked them for dinner
test: Dad says the film was tame. What does he mean? | It had lovely music and songs | It was very scary and dark | It was filmed in a jungle | *It was dull and not exciting
exam: «Not every animal can be tamed.» Which meaning fits tamed here? | Very, very old | Able to be painted | *Able to be trained to live with people | Always happy and smiling
